    <title>NYOP</title>
    <id>292917</id>
    <revision>
      <id>37396581</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-30T19:50:36Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Haza-w</username>
        <id>445993</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Stubbed. [[Wikipedia:WikiProject Stub sorting|You can help!]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''NYOP''' is an acronym for &quot;Name-Your-Own-Price&quot;, a system where a buyer specifies a price and a product and/or service, and asks sellers to match that combination.  NYOP is a special type of [[reverse auction]] originally pioneered on the [[Internet]] by [[priceline]].

[[Category:Auctioneering]]
{{Marketing-stub}}</text>
