      <text xml:space="preserve">''This is an article about a game [[company (law)|company]].  For information on the adventure [[computer game]] genre, please see [[adventure game]]''.

'''Adventure Games''' was a [[game]] manufacturer established in the early [[1980s]] by ''[[Dungeons &amp; Dragons]]'' co-author [[Dave Arneson]].  Some of Adventure Games' published works were:
* ''Johnny Reb''
* ''Harpoon''

It also published Arneson's ''Adventures in Fantasy'', which had been previously published by Excalibre Games.

Arneson decided to terminate the company and it became a division of [[Flying Buffalo]] in [[1985]].


