    <title>Nevado del Ruiz</title>
    <id>292993</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41383955</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-26T23:56:10Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Naconkantari</username>
        <id>676502</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Reverted edits by [[Special:Contributions/125.236.44.49|125.236.44.49]] ([[User talk:125.236.44.49|talk]]) to last version by Naconkantari</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;!-- BEGIN WikiProject Mountains infobox --&gt;
{{Mtnbox start | Name=Nevado del Ruiz |
      Photo=Nevado del Ruiz 1985.jpg | Caption=Steam eruption in September, 1985 |
      Elevation=5,389 metres (17,784 feet) |
      Location=[[Colombia]] | Range=[[Andes]]}}
{{Mtnbox coor dm|4|53|N|75|22|W|type:mountain}}
{{Mtnbox volcano|Type=[[Stratovolcano]] | Age=| Last eruption=[[1991]]}}
{{Mtnbox climb | First ascent=[[1936]] by [[M. Rapp]] and party |
      Easiest route=}}
{{Mtnbox finish}}
&lt;!-- END WikiProject Mountains infobox --&gt;

'''Nevado del Ruiz''' is a [[volcano]] in [[Colombia]].

On [[November 13]], [[1985]], Nevado del Ruiz erupted. [[Pyroclastic flow]]s melted ice and snow at the summit. This melt formed [[lahar]]s that rushed down several river valleys. The lahars were up to 50 meters thick and travelled more than 100 kilometres. 

Many houses and towns were devastated by the lahars. The town of [[Armero, Colombia]] was completely covered by debris. Approximately 21,000 people (out of 28,700) died in Armero. The eruption caused an estimated 25,000 deaths, 5,000 injuries, and destroyed more than 5,000 homes. This was the second-deadliest volcanic disaster in the [[20th century]] (the [[1902]] eruption of [[Mount Pelée]] was the worst).

Survivors who fled to other towns in the area were gradually housed in new government schemes, but problems for the displaced population occurred for many years after.

Even in the mid 1990s the town was covered with up to 20 feet of ash and debris. Local villagers harvested stones for building work and often, still, found human bones that they placed on the shrines that dot the area. A few small trees were trying to grow, protected from wandering animals by makeshift fences.

== External links and references ==
