      <minor />
      <comment>/* Singles */ rm link to &quot;Cold&quot; as it is not related to the song in any way</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">:''For the effect also called ''Crossfade'', see [[Crossfading]].''

'''Crossfade''' is a [[post grunge]] [[band (music)|band]] originating in [[Columbia, South Carolina]]. The group came together in [[1999]] with the merging of singer/guitarist Ed Sloan with bassist/backup singer Mitch James and drummer Brian Geiger as the power trio [[The Nothing]] and then the name was changed to Crossfade in [[2002]]. The group added singer and DJ Tony Byroads from [[Buffalo, New York]]. The resulting quartet renamed itself Sugardaddy Superstar. It first gained recognition beyond its region when it attracted the interest of the Los Angeles A&amp;R company Taxi. This ultimately led to the signing of a record deal with the Earshot division of [[Columbia Records]]. They released their first [[album (music)|album]] on [[April 13]] [[2004]]. 

The group is now a three-piece band as of spring [[2005]] due to the departure of the DJ/backing vocalist [[Tony Byroads]]. He wanted to spend time with his new bride. However, the group will continue touring and start doing work on their second full-length album that is due out sometime in [[2006]].

