  <page>
    <title>DMX</title>
    <id>293073</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41289292</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-26T08:31:15Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Lhademmor</username>
        <id>203383</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>+da</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''DMX''' has several meanings as an initialism or nickname:

* [[DMX (lighting)]] (&quot;Digital Multiplex&quot; or DMX-512), a lighting communications protocol
* [[DMX (rapper)]] (born 1970), alias for Earl Simmons, an African-American rapper/hip hop performer and actor
* [[DMX Krew]], alias for Ed Upton, an electronic music artist
* [[DMX Music]], formerly &quot;Digital Music Express&quot;, a subscription service that provides music in digital format in a variety of transmission modes
* [[DMX Sound Library]], a [[sound library]] used in the popular video game ''Doom''
* [[Dextromethorphan]] (DMX; also DM), an antitussive (anti-coughing) drug that is found in many over-the-counter cold and cough preparations
* [[5-dehydro-m-xylylene]], (DMX), the first known organic molecule to break [[Hund's rule]]
* [[Distributed Multiheaded X]]
* [[Data Mining Extensions]], a query language for data mining models defined in the OLEDB for DM standard
* Data Management, Exploration and Mining group in [[Microsoft]] Reasearch

{{wiktionary}}
{{TLAdisambig}}

[[da:DMX]]
[[es:DMX (desambiguación)]]
[[fr:DMX]]
[[nl:DMX]]</text>
