Lower Sorbian has both [[final devoicing]] and regressive [[phonation|voicing]] [[assimilation (linguistics)|assimilation]]:
*{{IPA|/dub/}} &quot;oak&quot; is pronounced {{IPA|[dup]}}
*{{IPA|/susedka/}} &quot;(female) neighbor&quot; is pronounced {{IPA|[susetka]}}
*{{IPA|/litsba/}} &quot;number&quot; is pronounced {{IPA|[lidzba]}}

The postalveolar fricative {{IPA|/ʃ/}} is assimilated to {{IPA|[ɕ]}} before {{IPA|/tɕ/}}:
*{{IPA|/ʃtɕit/}} &quot;protection&quot; is pronounced {{IPA|[ɕtɕit]}}

===Vowels===
The [[vowel]] phonemes are as follows:
