  <page>
    <title>The Pitts</title>
    <id>293163</id>
    <revision>
      <id>25677084</id>
      <timestamp>2005-10-16T19:07:17Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>205.188.116.197</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''''The Pitts''''' was a short-lived [[United States|American]] [[situation comedy|sitcom]] on [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]]. It is about a family and their bad luck.  Many people consider this to be one of the worst [[television program|TV shows]] ever made, although others consider it to be a fine example of high [[satire]].

''The Pitts'' is a term meant to imply that a place is the worst of the worst. ''The Pitts'' also is a [[nickname]] for [[Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania|Pittsburgh]] that some people find offensive.

==Episodes==

01. Pilot (aired [[March 30]], [[2003]])&lt;br&gt;
Bob hires a babysitter for the kids but doesn't realize she's the girl he stood up for prom night.

02. A Bug's Wife (aired [[April 6]], 2003)&lt;br&gt;
Faith gets a VW bug but it falls in love with her and plans to marry her in [[Las Vegas, Nevada|Vegas]].

03. Squarewolves (aired [[April 13]], 2003)&lt;br&gt;
Bob &amp; Liz turn into werewolves and wreak havoc in the nighttime.

04. Dummy &amp; Dummier (aired [[April 20]], 2003)&lt;br&gt;
A dummy comes to life and haunts the family.

05. Miss American Pipe (aired [[April 20]], 2003)&lt;br&gt;
Faith loses her chances of being in a rock video after a pipe goes through her head.

06. Bob's New Heart (didn't air)&lt;br&gt;
Bob &amp; Liz are conviced to join a dance club which turns out to be a satanic cult.

07. Ticket To Riot (didn't air)&lt;br&gt;
The Pitts take the wrong bus and are held hostage by escaping prisoners.

==External links==
* {{imdb title|id=0338647|title=The Pitts}}

[[Category:Fox network shows|Pitts]]
[[Category:Sitcoms|Pitts]]
{{tvseries-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Gigli</title>
    <id>293165</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41936650</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-02T19:16:18Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Ceejayoz</username>
        <id>48002</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Otheruses}} 

{{Infobox Film | name =Gigli
  | image    = Gigli (poster).jpg
  | caption  = DVD cover for ''Gigli''
  | director = [[Martin Brest]]		
  | producer = Martin Brest
  | writer   = Martin Brest
  | starring = [[Ben Affleck]]&lt;br&gt;[[Jennifer Lopez]]&lt;br&gt;[[Al Pacino]]&lt;br&gt;[[Christopher Walken]]&lt;br&gt;[[Lainie Kazan]]
  | music    = [[John Powell]]
  | cinematography = Robert Elswit
  | editing  = Julie Monroe&lt;br&gt;Billy Weber
  | distributor = [[Sony Pictures Entertainment|Sony]]&lt;br&gt;[[Revolution Studios|Revolution]] 
  | released = [[August 3]] [[2003 in film|2003]]
  | runtime  = 121 min
  | language = English 
  | budget   = $54 million
  | imdb_id  = 0299930
}}

'''''Gigli''''' (pronounced &quot;zhee-lee&quot;) is a film released in [[2003 in film|2003]] which was written and directed by [[Martin Brest]], starring [[Ben Affleck]] and [[Jennifer Lopez]]. [[Al Pacino]], [[Christopher Walken]], and [[Lainie Kazan]] also starred in the movie.

Originally a very dark comedy with no romantic subplot, the producers demanded script rewrites throughout filming.

In the final version of the film, Larry Gigli (Affleck) is a lowly thug who is tasked with the [[kidnapping]] of the [[mental retardation|mentally retarded]], ''[[Baywatch]]'' obsessed younger brother of a powerful federal [[prosecutor]], in an attempt to save his [[mobster]] boss from [[prison]].  The task proves to be difficult for Gigli, so Ricki (Lopez), a [[lesbian]] [[assassin]], is sent to oversee him.

== Reaction ==

The movie was considered a spectacular failure, with an opening weekend ranking of 7th, and having grossed less than [[United States dollar|$]]4 million in its opening weekend after costing $54 million to make, and earning nearly universally negative reviews.  (''Gigli'' also set a record for the biggest second-weekend drop in box office gross of any film in wide release since that statistic began to be kept; its gross dropped by almost 82% in its second weekend compared to its first. [http://www.boxofficemojo.com/alltime/weekends/drops.htm])  This public reaction led to its becoming a synonym for &quot;poor quality&quot; for a brief period in the summer of 2003, especially on late-night [[talk show]]s and was withdrawn from US theatres after only 3 weeks (one of the shortest circulation times for a big-budget movie), earning a total of only $6 million domestically and $1 million abroad. In terms of budget percentage, it is second only to [[Cutthroat Island]] (which cost almost $100 million, but earned only $10 million) as the biggest [[box-office bomb]] ever.

Although the film itself was widely seen as shockingly bad (with Lopez's &quot;It's turkey time&quot; sexual banter being the absolute low point), the media attention over Affleck and Lopez's [[engagement]] may have severely hampered the movie's reputation. Film critics were so fearsomely derisive that there was speculation as to whether they were competing to see who could give the nastiest review.

It has been suggested (particularly by the film's stars) that ''Gigli'' is not necessarily as bad as the reviews suggest, but rather happened to become a &quot;lightning rod&quot; film for public scorn, of a type that appears once every few years. Previous examples of films that became pariahs in the film industry may be found in [[Films considered the worst ever]].  Other examples include ''[[Heaven's Gate (film)|Heaven's Gate]]'' (1980), ''[[The Bonfire of the Vanities]]'' (1990), ''[[Hudson Hawk]]'' (1991), ''[[Far and Away]]'' (1992), ''[[Last Action Hero]]'' (1993), ''[[Waterworld]]'' (1995), ''[[Cutthroat Island]]'' (1995), ''[[The Postman]]'' (1997), ''[[Mortal Kombat: Annihilation]]'' (1997), and ''[[Freddy Got Fingered]]'' (2001).

The film received six [[Golden Raspberry Awards|Razzies]] in the [[2003 Golden Raspberry Awards]] &amp;ndash; Worst Picture, Worst Actor, Worst Actress, Worst Director, Worst Screenplay and Worst Screen Couple. Users of the [[Internet Movie Database]] have voted the film a prominent position on the site's list of the &quot;100 worst films ever made&quot;.

==External links==
*[http://www.sonypictures.com/movies/gigli/ Sony Pictures: ''Gigli'']
*{{imdb title|id=0299930|title=Gigli}}
*[http://www.agonybooth.com/gigli/ the agony booth : GIGLI Review]

[[Category:2003 films]]
[[Category:American films]]
[[Category:Flops]]
[[Category:Mafia comedies]]
[[Category:Worst Picture Razzie]]
[[fr:Amours troubles]]
[[no:Gigli]]
[[sv:Gigli]]</text>
    </revision>
