    <title>Jinul</title>
    <id>293196</id>
    <revision>
      <id>34620733</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-10T15:29:58Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Visviva</username>
        <id>123395</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{koreanname|
image=[[Image:JINUL.jpg|180px]]|
hangul=지눌|
hanja=知訥|
rr=Jinul|
mr=Chinul|
}}

'''Jinul''' ([[1158]] – [[1210]]) was a [[Korea|Korean]] monk of the [[Goryeo]] period, who is considered to be the most influential figure in the formation of Korean [[Seon]] [[Korean Buddhism|Buddhism]]. 

He was born at a time when the [[sangha]] was in a state of crisis, both in terms of its external reputation as well as on internal issues of doctrine. Deeply disturbed at the degree of corruption that had crept into the sangha, Jinul sought to establish a new movement within Korean Seon which he called the &quot;[[samadhi]] and [[prajna]] society&quot; (hanja: 定慧社, 정혜사, ''Jeonghyesa'').  This movement's goal was to establish a new community of disciplined, pure-minded practitioners deep in the mountains. Jinul eventually accomplished this mission with the founding of the [[Songgwangsa]] monastery at Mt. [[Jogye Mountain|Jogye]]. 

==See also==
* [[List of Korea-related topics]]
* [[Buddhism in Korea]]
* [[Korean philosophy]]

&lt;!-- I have removed an external link to the Digital Dictionary of Buddhism's main page. I have added a DDB link to the &quot;Korean buddhism&quot; article; the DDB is also linked from the &quot;Buddhism&quot; and &quot;Seon&quot; articles. I think that's plenty. User Talk:Wikipeditor --&gt;
[[Category:Korean Buddhism]]
[[Category:1158 births]]
[[Category:1210 deaths]]</text>
