    <title>Hollandse IJssel</title>
    <id>293199</id>
    <revision>
      <id>22617007</id>
      <timestamp>2005-09-05T12:12:47Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Agentsoo</username>
        <id>80866</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>disambiguation link repair ([[Wikipedia:Disambiguation pages with links|You can help!]])</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[image:RhineUtrecht.jpg|thumb|right|[[Satellite]] [[image]] of the [[Rhine]] branches around the [[city]] of [[Utrecht (city)|Utrecht]] showing the upper stretch of [[river]] Hollandse IJssel (f).]]The '''Hollandse IJssel''' (&quot;[[Holland]] IJssel&quot;, as opposed to the 'regular' or [[Gelderland]] [[IJssel]]) is a branch of the [[Rhine]] [[river delta|delta]] that flows westward from  [[Nieuwegein]] on [[river]] [[Lek River|Lek]] through [[IJsselstein]], [[Gouda]] and [[Capelle aan den IJssel]] to [[Krimpen aan den IJssel]], where it ends in the [[Nieuwe Maas]]. Another branch called Enge IJssel (&quot;Narrow IJssel&quot;) flows southwest from Nieuwegein. The name IJssel is thought to derive from the [[Germanic languages|Germanic]] &lt;em&gt;i sala&lt;/em&gt;, meaning &quot;dark [[water]]&quot;. Originally, the Hollandse IJssel forked off from river Lek at Nieuwegein, but the connection was cut off with the Hollandse IJssel nowadays only draining the surrounding [[pasture]]s.

[[image:RMSDeltaNorth.jpg|thumb|left|Satellite image of the northwestern part of the [[Rhine]]-[[Meuse river|Meuse]] [[river delta|delta]] showing the lower stretch of river Hollandse IJssel (m).]]The first part of the [[Delta Works]] sea protection constructions was built at the mouth of the Hollandse IJssel in [[1957]].

==See also==
* [[IJssel]]
----
