    <title>DIN 31635</title>
    <id>293204</id>
    <revision>
      <id>35552092</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-17T16:17:51Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Dbachmann</username>
        <id>86857</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''DIN 31635''' is a [[DIN]] standard for the [[transliteration]] of the [[Arabic alphabet]].

:The 28 ''{{ArabDIN|ḫuruf}}: ''{{ArabDIN|ʾ/ā, b, t, ṯ, ǧ, ḥ, ḫ, d, ḏ, r, z, s, š, ṣ, ḍ, ṭ, ẓ, ʿ, ġ, f, q, k, l, m, n, h, w/ū, y/ī.}}

The [[Harakat]], {{ArabDIN|fatḥa}},  {{ArabDIN|kasra}} and {{ArabDIN|ḍamma}} are transliterated as {{ArabDIN|a}}, {{ArabDIN|i}}, {{ArabDIN|u}}. A [[shadda|šadda]] results in a [[geminate]] (consonant written twice), except in the case of the article, which is written with  &quot;Sun letters&quot; assimilated ({{ArabDIN|aš-šamsu}}).
An [[alif]] marking {{IPA|[a:]}} is transliterated as {{ArabDIN|ā}}. {{ArabDIN|tāʼ marbūṭa}} ({{ar|ﺓ}}) as word-final {{ArabDIN|-h}} or {{ArabDIN|-t}}.
{{ArabDIN|ʾalif makṣūra}} ({{ar|ﻯ}}) appears as {{ArabDIN|ā}}, rendering it indistinguishable from alif.
Long vowels {{IPA|[i:]}} and {{IPA|[u:]}} are transliterated as {{ArabDIN|ī}} and {{ArabDIN|ū}}. The [[Nisba]] suffix appears as {{ArabDIN|-iyy-}}, nunation is written as simple {{ArabDIN|-un}}, {{ArabDIN|-an}}, {{ArabDIN|-in}}. A hyphen {{ArabDIN|-}} is used to separate morphological elements, notably the article and prepositions. 

The &quot;Arabic-Indic numerals&quot; in use with the Arabic alphabet ({{ar|٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩}}) are rendered as western &quot;[[Arabic numerals]]&quot; ({{ArabDIN|0123456789}}).


== See also ==

*[[Arabic transliteration]]
* [[ISO 233]]

== External links ==
* [http://ee.www.ee/transliteration/pdf/Arabic.pdf Arabic script]
* [http://www.omniglot.com/writing/arabic.htm Standard order of the Arabic alphabet]


{{standard-stub}}

[[Category:Romanization]]
[[Category:DIN standards]]
[[Category:Arabic alphabet]]</text>
    </revision>
