|}

==Persons==

São Tomé is home to the two presidents of the nation including [[Miguel Trovoada]] and [[Fradique de Menezes]].

==Other==
São Tomé has schools, middle schools, high schools, churches, a beach, an airport, São Tomé and Príncipe's only hospital and a television station  [[RFI (Television network)|RFI]], radio stations and squares (''[[praça]]s'')

São Tomé is also the name given to the Indian city of [[Chennai]] by the early Portugese visitors in 1522.

