    <id>293242</id>
    <revision>
      <id>39251555</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-11T21:35:45Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>83.121.7.181</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>disambiguation from [[John Fletcher]] to [[John Fletcher (playwright)]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The '''''Golden Treasury of English Songs and Lyrics''''' is a popular [[anthology]] of [[English language|English]] [[poetry]], originally selected for publication by [[Francis Turner Palgrave]] in [[1861]]. It was considerably revised, with input from [[Alfred Tennyson, 1st Baron Tennyson|Tennyson]], about three decades later.

The book continues to be published in regular new editions, still under Palgrave's name.

==Book I (Palgrave)==

[[William Alexander, 1st Earl of Stirling]] - [[R. Barnefield]] - [[T. Campion]] - [[S. Daniel]] - [[T. Dekker]] - [[R. Devereux, Earl of Essex]] - [[J. Donne]] - [[M. Drayton]] - [[W. Drummond]] - [[W. Drummond of Hawthornden]] - [[R. Greene]] - [[T. Heywood]] - [[T. Lodge]] - [[J. Lylye]] - [[C. Marlowe]] - [[T. Nash]] - [[W. Shakespeare]] - [[Sir P. Sidney]] - [[E. Spenser]] - [[The Shepherd Tonie]] - [[J. Sylvester]] - [[J. Webster]] - Sir [[Thomas Wyatt]]

==Book II (Palgrave)==

[[Francis Beaumont]] - [[Thomas Carew]] - [[A. Cowley]] - [[Richard Crashaw]] - [[J. Dryden]] - [[John Fletcher (playwright)|John Fletcher]] - [[W. Habington]] - [[George Herbert]] - [[Robert Herrick]] - [[B. Jonson]] - [[Colonel Lovelace]] - [[Andrew Marvell]] - [[J. Milton]] - [[J. Norris of Bemerton]] - [[Francis Quarles]] - Sir [[Charles Sedley]] - [[John Shirley]] - Sir [[John Suckling]] - [[Henry Vaughan]] - [[E. Waller]] - [[John Wilmot, Earl of Rochester]] - [[G. Wither]] - Sir [[Henry Wotton]]

