    <title>Conseil de l'Entente</title>
    <id>293256</id>
    <revision>
      <id>37006204</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-27T22:49:37Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>RevAustin</username>
        <id>344769</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Fixed the part where it says Abidjan is the capital of Côte d'Ivoire.</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The '''Conseil de l'Entente''' (&quot;Council of Accord&quot; or &quot;Council of Understanding&quot;) is a [[West Africa]]n regional co-operation forum established in May [[1959]] by [[Côte d'Ivoire]], [[Niger]], [[Burkina Faso]] and [[Benin]], and joined in [[1996]] by [[Togo]]. 

The body grew out of the short-lived [[Sahel-Benin Union]], itself created by the four original Council members as a partial successor to the dissolved [[France|French]] regional colonial federation of [[French West Africa]]. 

Since [[1966]] the Council has possessed a permanent administrative Secretariat based in [[Abidjan]], the largest city of Côte d'Ivoire. A Mutual Aid and Loan Guarantee Fund exists to assist poorer members from a common pool.

==See also==
*[[Entente]]
*[[Trade bloc]]
*[[International organization]]s

{{africa-stub}}
[[Category:1959 in law]]</text>
    </revision>
