  <page>
    <title>Syndicate</title>
    <id>293273</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41641028</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-28T18:59:40Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>72.17.139.211</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* [[Mass media]] */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{dablink|This article is about the association term. See ''[[Syndicate (computer game series)|Syndicate]]'' for an article about the computer game of the same name, or [[Syndicate (X-files)]] for the fictional organization.}}
==Common usage==
A '''syndicate''' is an association of people or companies. 

==Etymology==
The word comes from [[French language|French]] ''syndicat'' which means ''administrator'' especially in matters regarding a certain geographical area, from the [[Latin]] word ''syndicus'' which in turn comes from the [[Greek language|Greek]] word σύνδικος (''syndikos'') which means ''caretaker of an issue'', compare to [[ombudsman]] or [[representative]].

==French==
In the original [[French language]] this word is mostly used for [[labor union|trade union]]s, but in common vocabulary it has extended to encompass also [[trust]]s, [[crime ring|ring]]s, [[cartel]]s and other (spontaneous) business associations as well.

==[[Crime syndicate]]s== 
Crime syndicates are criminal groups running common businesses. 

==[[Mass media]]==
In the [[mass media]], a syndicate will offer work for [[syndication]].

{{wiktionary}}

[[de:Syndikat]]
[[el:σύνδικος]]
[[fr:Syndicat]]
[[no:Syndikat]]
[[nl:Syndicaat]]
[[pl:Syndykat]]
[[sr:Синдикат]]
[[sv:Syndikat]]</text>
    </revision>
