  <page>
    <title>Johann Peter Lange</title>
    <id>293354</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40211122</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-19T00:02:00Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Yms</username>
        <id>849938</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Johann Peter Lange''' ([[April 10]], [[1802]] - [[July 9]], [[1884]]), was a [[Germany|German]] [[Protestant]] [[theology|theologian]] of peasant origin and was born at Sonneborn near [[Elberfeld]].

He studied [[theology]] at [[University of Bonn|Bonn]] (from 1822) under [[Karl Immanuel Nitzsch|KI Nitzsch]] and [[Gottfried Christian Friedrich Lücke|GCF Lücke]], held several pastorates, and eventually (1854) settled at Bonn as professor of theology in succession to [[Isaac August Dorner]], becoming also in [[1860]] counsellor to the consistory.

Lange has been called the poetical theologian ''par excellence'': &quot;It has been said of him that his thoughts succeed each other in such rapid and agitated waves that all calm reflection and all rational distinction become, in a manner, drowned&quot; (F Lichtenberger).

As a [[dogma]]tic writer he belonged to the school of [[Friedrich Daniel Ernst Schleiermacher|Schleiermacher]]. His ''Christliche Dogmatics'' (5 vols, 1849-1852, new edition, 1870) &quot;contains many fruitful and suggestive thoughts, which, however, are hidden under such a mass of bold figures and strange fancies and suffer so much from want of clearness of presentation, that they did not produce any lasting effect&quot; ([[Otto Pfleiderer]]).

His other works include ''Das Leben Jesu'' (3 vols, 1844-1847), ''Das apostolische Zeitalter'' (2 vols, 1853-1854), ''Grundriss der theologischen Encyklopädie'' (1877), ''Grundriss der christlichen Ethik'' (1878), and ''Grundriss der Bibelkunde'' (1881). In 1857 he undertook with other scholars a ''Theologisch-homiletisches Bibelwerk'', to which he contributed commentaries on the first four books of the [[Pentateuch]], [[Haggai]], [[Zechariah]], [[Malachi]], [[Gospel of Matthew|Matthew]], [[Gospel of Mark|Mark]], [[book of Revelation|Revelation]]. The ''Bibelwerk'' has been translated, enlarged and revised under the general editorship of [[Philip Schaff]].

==References==
*{{1911}}
[[Category:1802 births|Lange, Johann Peter]]
[[Category:1884 deaths|Lange, Johann Peter]]
[[Category:German theologians|Lange, Johann Peter]]

[[de:Johann Peter Lange]]
[[ru:Ланге, Иоганн Петер]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Mac OS X v10.3</title>
    <id>293355</id>
    <revision>
      <id>37007666</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-27T23:01:46Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>142.68.204.13</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Infobox OS|
| name = Mac OS X v10.3 &quot;Panther&quot;
| screenshot = [[Image:AM MacOSX Panther.png|256px|A screenshot of Mac OS X v10.3 &quot;Panther&quot;.]]
| caption = A screenshot of Mac OS X v10.3 &quot;Panther&quot;.
| developer = [[Apple Computer]]
| family = [[BSD]]
| source_model = [[Closed source]] ([[Darwin (operating system)|Darwin]] foundation is [[open source]])
| latest_release_version = 10.3.9
| latest_release_date = [[April 15]] [[2005]]
| kernel_type = [[XNU]] (based upon [[Mach kernel|Mach]])
| license = [[Apple Public Source License|APSL]] and Apple [[EULA]]
| working_state = Supported
| website = http://www.apple.com/support/panther/
}}
'''Mac OS X version 10.3 &quot;Panther&quot;''' is the fourth major release of [[Apple Computer]]'s [[Mac OS X]] [[operating system]]. It follows [[Mac OS X v10.2]] &quot;Jaguar&quot; and precedes [[Mac OS X v10.4]] &quot;Tiger&quot;.

Apple released Panther on [[October 24]], [[2003]]. The cost from Apple was US$129.00 for a single-user license and US$199.00 for a Family Pack (5 user, 1 household) license.

Apple advertises that Panther has at least 150 new features, including:

*[[Macintosh Finder|Finder]] updated interface
**Brushed-metal interface
**Real-time searching (like [[iTunes]])
**Customizable sidebar (like iTunes)
*[[Fast User Switching]], that allows a user to remain logged in while another user logs in feature, featuring the desktop on an animated cube (the effect is only seen on systems with [[Quartz Compositor#Quartz Extreme|Quartz Extreme]]). [[Windows XP]] has a similar feature without an animated cube.
* [[Exposé (Mac OS X)|Exposé]], a program to help the user manage windows, especially large numbers of them.
* [[Fax]] support built-in.
*[[ZIP (file format)|Zip]] support built in.
* [[X11.app|X11]] support built-in.
* [[TextEdit]] support for [[Microsoft Word]] (*.doc) documents.
*[[Microsoft Windows]] interoperability improvements, including support for [[SecurID]]-based [[VPN]]s.
* Security
**[[FileVault]]: on the fly [[encryption]] and decryption of a user's [[home folder]]
**Secure deletion
* [[Xcode]] Developer Tools, which speeds [[compile]] times greatly with [[GNU Compiler Collection|gcc]] 3.3.
*[[iChat AV]] [[Video teleconference|video-conferencing]] software
*[[Portable Document Format|PDF]] rendering speed increase
*[[File label]]s
*[[Pixlet]] high definition [[video codec]]

10.3 (Panther) has increased system requirements over 10.2 (Jaguar) as it requires the computer to have a USB port. This change in requirements means that beige Power Mac G3s and wallstreet PowerBook G3s are unable to run 10.3. Checks are made during the install process and hence installation will fail on older machines. This requirement can be overcome by using 3rd party software such as Xpostfacto.

==Version history==
* Mac OS X v10.3.0 (build 7B85), released [[24 October]] [[2003]] (retail)
* Mac OS X v10.3.1 (build 7C107), released [[10 November]] [[2003]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate_10_3_1.html Apple Download Page])
* Mac OS X v10.3.2 (build 7D24), released [[17 December]] [[2003]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate_10_3_2.html Apple Download Page])
* Mac OS X v10.3.3 (build 7F44), released [[15 March]] [[2004]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate_10_3_3.html Apple Download Page])
* Mac OS X v10.3.4 (build 7H63), released [[26 May]] [[2004]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate_10_3_4.html Apple Download Page])
* Mac OS X v10.3.5 (build 7M34), released [[8 August]] [[2004]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate_10_3_5.html Apple Download Page])
* Mac OS X v10.3.6 (build 7R28), released [[5 November]] [[2004]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate_10_3_6.html Apple Download Page])
* Mac OS X v10.3.7 (build 7S215), released [[15 December]] [[2004]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate_10_3_7.html Apple Download Page])
* Mac OS X v10.3.8 (build 7U16), released [[9 February]] [[2005]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate1038.html Apple Download Page])
* Mac OS X v10.3.9 (build 7W98), released [[15 April]] [[2005]] ([http://www.apple.com/downloads/macosx/apple/macosxupdate1039.html Apple Download Page])

